{"v":1,"id":["01KZPTN6CSW9RYMDP5S8X3TA6C","01KZPTN5N6W1KNRXSX9M37A4N1"],"edit.description":{"id":"01KZPTMY7JCQ24YHX1Z3DTQKMH","md":"Requirement (user, verbatim intent): the scrubber currently spaces frames by real elapsed time, which leaves \"empty void\" gaps where no activity happened. Add two toggleable layout modes:\n\n1. **Real spacing** (current behavior) — frames positioned proportionally to actual time elapsed, gaps visible where history is quiet.\n2. **Even frames** (new, becomes the default) — every non-empty bucket gets equal width, laid out as a contiguous stacked filmstrip with no gaps, regardless of real time between them.\n\nNeeds a UI control to toggle between the two modes. Default mode changes from the current always-real-spacing behavior to even-frames."}}
